WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.070
You're Robert Cornelius.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:03.855
Philadelphia, 1839.

00:00:03.955 --> 00:00:05.966
Photography is brand new.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.306
Daguerre announced his
method in France only

00:00:08.316 --> 00:00:09.356
that August.

00:00:09.366 --> 00:00:11.730
You work in your family's lamp business,

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.994
and you're an expert at silver plating.

00:00:14.004 --> 00:00:14.837
Your camera?

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:16.387
A box, with a lens from an

00:00:16.397 --> 00:00:17.573
opera glass.

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:19.578
Indoors is too dark, so you set

00:00:19.588 --> 00:00:22.174
up outside, behind the family store.

00:00:22.184 --> 00:00:23.957
Uncover the lens, get in front of

00:00:23.967 --> 00:00:25.298
it, and hold still.

00:00:25.308 --> 00:00:26.623
This is the real one, at the

00:00:26.633 --> 00:00:28.358
Library of Congress.

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:31.401
Hair messy, arms crossed,
a little off-centre.

00:00:31.411 --> 00:00:32.948
On the back you wrote:

00:00:32.958 --> 00:00:35.588
"The first light picture ever taken.

00:00:35.598 --> 00:00:36.112
1839."

00:00:36.237 --> 00:00:38.224
Guinness calls it the first selfie.

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:40.511
Months later, you open one of America's

00:00:40.521 --> 00:00:42.399
first photo studios.

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:44.359
Not bad for a lamp maker.
